<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Bellovaci</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Bratuspantium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The most powerful of the Belgic peoples, around Beauvais, who fought Caesar in 57 BCE and led one of the last Gallic revolts in 51 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bellovaci lived in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oise-department">Oise</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beauvais">Beauvais</a>. Caesar was told that they could field a hundred thousand men and had promised sixty thousand to the Belgic league of 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their society was led by a warrior nobility, and they had ties to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aedui">Aedui</a>. Large sanctuaries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gournay-sur-aronde">Gournay-sur-Aronde</a>, with displays of weapons and sacrificed animals, show their religious practice.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 57 BCE they surrendered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratuspantium">Bratuspantium</a> after the Aeduan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diviciacus-aedui">Diviciacus</a> spoke for them. In 51 BCE they rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/correus">Correus</a>, who died fighting. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beauvais">Caesaromagus</a>, later Beauvais.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bellovaci.jpg" alt="Bellovaci" width="320" height="299"><figcaption>Image: The Department of History, United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaul,_1st_century_BC.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bratuspantium</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Correus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=bellovaci" aria-label="Bellovaci on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4733 524 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bellovaci lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5053 780h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5053 780h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=bellovaci">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

